      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Introduction to Latent Semantic Analysis\n2\nAbstract\nLatent Semantic Analysis (LSA) is a theory and method for extracting and representing the\ncontextual-usage meaning of words by statistical computations applied to a large corpus of\ntext (Landauer and Dumais, 1997). The underlying idea is that the aggregate of all the word\ncontexts in which a given word does and does not appear provides a set of mutual\nconstraints that largely determines the similarity of meaning of words and sets of words to\n\u0000\u0002\u0001\u0004\u0003\u0002\u0005\u0007\u0006\t\b\n\u0005\t\u0000\u0002\u000b\r\f\u000f\u000e\u0010\u0005\t\u0000\u0011\u0001\u0002\u0012\t\u0000\u0004\u0013\u0015\u0014\t\u0001\u0004\u0003\u0002\u0016\u0007\u0006\u0015\u0017\u0019\u0018\u001b\u001a\u001d\u001c\u001f\u001e \u000b!\u0000\u0004\u0017!\"\n\u0000\u0004\u0003\u0002\b\n#\n\u0006\t$\u0007\u0006\u0015\u0017\u0019\u0005\t\u0014\u0015%&\u0001\u0004$\u0007'\u0015$\t\u0006\t()\"\n\u0000\u0002\u0012",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Abstract introducing Latent Semantic Analysis (LSA) as a theory and statistical method for extracting and representing the contextual-usage meaning of words from a large text corpus (Landauer & Dumais, 1997), based on the mutual constraints provided by the aggregate of word contexts in which a word does and does not appear. Notes that LSA scores overlap human scores on standard vocabulary and subject-matter tests, mimic human word-sorting and category judgments, and accurately estimate passage coherence, passage learnability for individual students, and the quality and quantity of knowledge in an essay (two multi-line spans in the extracted text are garbled by PDF font encoding).",
