      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Introduction to Latent Semantic Analysis\n5\nwords, or that their words have reflected such matters unintentionally, LSA has at least\npotential access to knowledge about them. The representations of passages that LSA forms\n\u0003\u0002\u0001\u0004$1+\t\u0000\u0011#\n$\u0015\b\n\u0000\u0004\u000b!2\t\u000b!\u0000\u0002\b\n\u0000\u0004\u00121\u0001\u0002\u001e \u0001\u0002+\t\u001e-\b4\u000b0\u0001\u0002\u0003\u0002\b\n#\n\u0006\t$\t\u001e8\u0006\t\u0017\n\r\u0019\u0000\u00022\t#\n\u001e-\u0006\u0015\u0012\t\u0000\u0002\u001e\n\u000f\u00197\n\u001e-\u0006\u0015%&\u0000\u0004\b4#\n%&\u0000\u0004\u001e\n\u0006\u0015\u0017\u0019\u0000\u00022\t#4\u001e-\u0006\t\u0012\t\u0000\u0002\u001e8\u0006\t\u0017\n2\t\u0014\t\u000b!\u0000\u0002\"\n\u0016\n\u0001\n\u0000\u0004\u000b!+\t\u0001\u0002\"\ncontent such as philosophical arguments, and sometimes episodes from real or imagined\nlife coded into verbal descriptions.  Its representation of words, in turn, is intertwined with\n\u0001\u0002$\t\u0012\u0007%&\u0014\u0015\b\n\u0014\t\u0001\u0004\"\n\"\n\u00161#\n$\t\b\n\u0000\u0002\u000b0\u0012\u0015\u0000\u00042\t\u0000\u0002$\t\u0012\t\u0000",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues discussing what text-only LSA representations capture (including philosophical arguments and verbal descriptions of life episodes, with several lines garbled by font encoding) and notes LSA's further limitations: it makes no use of word order, syntax, logic, or morphology. Contrasts LSA with other statistical approaches in two key respects, explaining the first here: LSA's initial input associations are between unitary expressions of meaning—words and the complete meaningful utterances (sentences or paragraphs treated as unitary wholes) in which they occur—rather than contiguous pairwise co-occurrences between successive words, thus relating word-choice differences to passage-meaning differences without modeling word order.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
