      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Illustrates how SVD estimates word occurrences from a passage's and word's loadings on two abstract concepts, and analyzes how dimension reduction reshapes word–word and title–title relations in Figures 1, 3, and 4. For word–word relations, human never co-occurs in the same title with either user or minors (raw correlations -.38 and -.29), yet in the 2D reconstruction indirect contextual relations raise the human–user correlation to .94 and lower human–minors to -.83. For title–title relations in the raw data, correlations among the five HCI titles average only .02, among the four graph-theory titles .44, and between the two disjoint groups -.30.",
