        "text": "Reports that all five LSA essay-scoring methods correlated with expert-assigned grades approximately as well as—and in a meta-analysis of eight exams across heart anatomy/physiology, psychology, American history, social issues, and marketing using Method 1 (Laham, 1997a), significantly better than—individual expert graders (ETS readers or course instructors) correlated with one another. Notes the counter-intuitive implication that conveying conceptual knowledge in an essay relies primarily on word choice rather than syntactic structure, and opens \"LSA and Text Comprehension,\" reviewing how Kintsch and colleagues (van Dijk & Kintsch, 1983; Kintsch & Vipond, 1979; McNamara et al., 1996) measured discourse coherence via argument overlap in hand-coded propositional representations.",
