        "text": "Explains how Foltz, Kintsch, and Landauer (1993, 1998/this issue; Foltz, 1996) replaced labor-intensive hand propositionalization with automatic LSA coherence measurement—computing cosines between successive sentences or passages—which predicted reader comprehension scores on a set of cardiac texts at r = .93 and automatically pinpoints coherence breakdowns and semantic shifts. Opens \"Predicting learning from text,\" summarizing how Rehder et al. and Wolfe et al. (1998/this issue), building on Kintsch's (1994; McNamara et al., 1996) zone-of-learnability findings, use LSA cosines between a student's short pre-reading essay and candidate instructional texts to match readers with texts of optimal conceptual complexity and position texts along a conceptual continuum.",
