        "text": "Argues that although the human brain is unlikely to compute SVD literally, it must apply comparable analytic power to turn local experiences into global knowledge, and that LSA offers a mathematically explicit path for theories of mind grounded in representative data rather than mentalistic primitives. Outlines directions for improving LSA—training on larger, more representative corpora of written and spoken language, incorporating non-linguistic experience, coupling LSA representations with dynamic online comprehension models such as Kintsch's Construction-Integration architecture (Kintsch, 1998), and representing word order in the input data (as in Burgess & Lund, 1998/this issue)—while noting that current applications remain constrained by non-optimal training corpora.",
